From: Iltix <dev@iltix.de>
Date: Sat, 19 Apr 2026 00:00:03 +0000
Subject: Iltix Module: Navigation — Custom Bottom Nav Bar

Implements the Iltix Navigation module:
- Separates the URL bar from the navigation button row
- Replaces the navigation area with a 7-button layout (left to right):
    ← Back | → Forward | ↻ Reload | 🏠 Home | 🧩 Extensions | [N] Tabs | ⋮ Menu
- Reuses the existing Chromium tab counter drawable for the Tabs button
- Reuses the existing extension toolbar button action for Extensions
- The Home button navigates to the user's configured homepage

The module is gated by IltixModuleManager.isNavigationEnabled().
When disabled, the bar renders exactly as stock Cromite.

The URL/omnibox bar position (top or bottom) is controlled by Cromite's
existing MoveTopToolbarToBottom flag — this module does not change that.

Requires: Iltix-Module-Settings-Infrastructure.patch

